{"skill":{"slug":"apple-reminders","displayName":"Apple Reminders"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545296326,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2310,"sha256":"0cbe33ba91010d54e2c53e20500ffc1fd8320b507b1ba8fcb5cf3170487a5918","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1898,"sha256":"4fa61a36680a1550e61cecb20768c67d888524cc937f72dd84753ce1bb6974af","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013561356,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d77e75c919d892fd58f7b18bfee7751a2a2a1729393d24343de9e6b88453a49d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d77e75c919d892fd58f7b18bfee7751a2a2a1729393d24343de9e6b88453a49d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: apple-reminders\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed to manage Apple Reminders using the `remindctl` CLI tool. The `SKILL.md` file specifies installation via Homebrew (`brew install steipete/tap/remindctl`), which is a standard and generally safe method for installing macOS command-line tools. All described commands are legitimate uses of `remindctl` for managing reminders. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, prompt injection attempts against the agent, or obfuscation. The behavior is clearly aligned with its stated purpose and lacks high-risk activities beyond standard CLI tool interaction.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159605870},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":9,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789013561356},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Apple Reminders helper, with expected reminder-management powers but limited warnings around delete commands.","dimensions":[{"detail":"macOS Reminders access is necessary for the stated purpose, and the skill discloses the permission prompt and System Settings location.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation uses a disclosed Homebrew tap for remindctl or a source build path with pnpm; no bundled executable script or hidden installer behavior appears in the artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions are direct command examples for user-requested reminder operations; the delete-list and force-delete-reminder examples are explicit but should better warn users to verify targets first.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact does not instruct background agents, services, hooks, memory writes, credential collection, or privilege escalation; any installed CLI and Reminders permission are expected for this integration.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is to manage Apple Reminders through remindctl, and its documented capabilities match that purpose, including creating, editing, completing, listing, and deleting reminders or lists.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Before installing, be aware this skill can help an agent change and delete Apple Reminders on a Mac after Reminders permission is granted. Use deletion commands only after confirming the target reminder ID or list name, especially commands using --force or --delete.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The force-delete reminder example is purpose-aligned and user-visible, but it lacks a caution that deletion may be irreversible and that the reminder ID should be checked first.\n[SQP-2] expected: The list deletion example is consistent with a reminder-management skill, but users should confirm the list name and contents before running it because it can remove multiple reminders.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013561356}}}}}